## Domain Layer Testing Pattern

### Table-Driven Tests
Use table-driven tests for comprehensive validation coverage:

```go
func TestUser_Validate(t *testing.T) {
    tests := []struct {
        name    string
        user    *User
        wantErr bool
        errType error
    }{
        {
            name: "valid user",
            user: &User{ID: "123", Name: "John Doe", Email: "john@example.com"},
            wantErr: false,
        },
        {
            name: "missing ID",
            user: &User{Name: "John Doe", Email: "john@example.com"},
            wantErr: true,
            errType: ErrInvalidUserID,
        },
    }

    for _, tt := range tests {
        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {
            err := tt.user.Validate()
            if tt.wantErr {
                assert.Error(t, err)
                if tt.errType != nil {
                    assert.ErrorIs(t, err, tt.errType)
                }
            } else {
                assert.NoError(t, err)
            }
        })
    }
}
```

### Domain Entity Testing
Test business rules and validation logic in isolation:

```go
func TestUser_String(t *testing.T) {
    user := &User{
        ID:    "123",
        Name:  "John Doe",
        Email: "john@example.com",
    }

    expected := "User{ID: 123, Name: John Doe, Email: john@example.com}"
    assert.Equal(t, expected, user.String())
}
```

## Use Case Layer Testing Pattern

### Mock-Based Testing
Test use cases with mocked dependencies following the pattern from [internal/usecase/user_test.go](mdc:gRPC-server/internal/usecase/user_test.go):

```go
func TestUserUseCase_CreateUser(t *testing.T) {
    mockRepo := mocks.NewMockUserRepository()
    mockValidator := mocks.NewMockUserValidator()
    mockLogger := mocks.NewMockLogger()
    mockPublisher := mocks.NewMockEventPublisher()

    useCase := NewUserUseCase(mockRepo, mockValidator, mockLogger, mockPublisher)

    user := testutil.NewValidUser()

    err := useCase.CreateUser(context.Background(), user)
    assert.NoError(t, err)

    // Verify interactions
    assert.Equal(t, 1, mockValidator.ValidateCallCount())
    assert.Equal(t, 1, mockRepo.CreateCallCount())
    assert.Equal(t, 1, mockPublisher.PublishCallCount())
}
```

### Error Scenario Testing
Test all error paths and edge cases:

```go
func TestUserUseCase_CreateUser_ValidationError(t *testing.T) {
    mockRepo := mocks.NewMockUserRepository()
    mockValidator := mocks.NewMockUserValidator()
    mockValidator.SetValidateError(domain.ErrInvalidUserEmail)

    useCase := NewUserUseCase(mockRepo, mockValidator, nil, nil)

    user := testutil.NewInvalidUser()

    err := useCase.CreateUser(context.Background(), user)
    assert.ErrorIs(t, err, domain.ErrInvalidUserEmail)

    // Repository should not be called
    assert.Equal(t, 0, mockRepo.CreateCallCount())
}
```

## Mock Implementation Patterns

### Thread-Safe Mocks
Implement thread-safe mocks for concurrent testing based on [internal/mocks/user_repository_mock.go](mdc:gRPC-server/internal/mocks/user_repository_mock.go):

```go
type MockUserRepository struct {
    mu             sync.RWMutex
    users          map[string]*domain.User
    createCalls    int
    getByIDCalls   int
    createError    error
    getByIDError   error
}

func (m *MockUserRepository) Create(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error {
    m.mu.Lock()
    defer m.mu.Unlock()

    m.createCalls++

    if m.createError != nil {
        return m.createError
    }

    m.users[user.ID] = user
    return nil
}
```

### Configurable Mock Behavior
Allow mocks to simulate different scenarios:

```go
func (m *MockUserRepository) SetCreateError(err error) {
    m.mu.Lock()
    defer m.mu.Unlock()
    m.createError = err
}

func (m *MockUserRepository) CreateCallCount() int {
    m.mu.RLock()
    defer m.mu.RUnlock()
    return m.createCalls
}
```

## Test Utilities and Factories

### Test Data Factories
Create reusable test data factories in [internal/testutil/helpers.go](mdc:gRPC-server/internal/testutil/helpers.go):

```go
func NewValidUser() *domain.User {
    return &domain.User{
        ID:    "test-123",
        Name:  "Test User",
        Email: "test@example.com",
    }
}

func NewUserWithID(id string) *domain.User {
    user := NewValidUser()
